### IntelliJ HTTP client: click the ▶ next to each request.
### Keycloak must be running on http://localhost:8180 (see README, section 3a).
@base = http://localhost:8080/api/v1

### 1. Log in (admin can do everything; try planner / supervisor / viewer too)
POST http://localhost:8180/realms/manufacturing/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=manufacturing-cli&username=admin&password=admin123

> {% client.global.set("token", response.body.access_token); %}

### List plants
GET {{base}}/plants
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Create a plant
POST {{base}}/plants
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "JP-TCG-01",
  "name": "Tochigi Assembly Plant",
  "city": "Kaminokawa",
  "country": "Japan",
  "dailyCapacity": 700
}

### Create a vehicle model
POST {{base}}/vehicle-models
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "modelCode": "ZEN-SEDAN",
  "name": "Zen Sedan",
  "category": "SEDAN",
  "powertrain": "HYBRID",
  "launchYear": 2026,
  "basePrice": 3150000.00
}

### Create a production order (use ids returned above)
POST {{base}}/production-orders
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "plantId": 1,
  "vehicleModelId": 1,
  "quantity": 3000,
  "priority": "HIGH",
  "plannedStartDate": "2026-12-01",
  "plannedEndDate": "2026-12-10",
  "notes": "Year-end dealer allocation"
}

### Start the order (replace 4 with the id returned by the create request)
PATCH {{base}}/production-orders/4/status
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "IN_PROGRESS" }

### Report progress
PATCH {{base}}/production-orders/4/progress
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "completedQuantity": 1200 }

### Filter orders
GET {{base}}/production-orders?status=IN_PROGRESS&plantId=1&sort=priority,desc
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
